      <w:r>
        <w:t>very weekday morning a wave moves along the ring road. It is not water but traffic: a band of slow cars that starts near the harbour bridge and travels backwards, against the flow, at about eighteen kilometres an hour. Drivers caught in it see brake lights appear from nowhere; drivers behind it never learn why the road suddenly slowed.</w:t>
      </w:r>
    </w:p>
    <w:p>
