      <w:r>
        <w:t>The table shows the average error in vehicles per kilometre. In free flow both methods do well: the road is empty enough that little can go wrong. As traffic thickens, the detectors alone fall behind, because a queue can grow for minutes before it reaches a loop.</w:t>
